course: dictionary
lesson: 5351
title: Kilometre, a long distance
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A kilometre is a unit for measuring long distances. One kilometre is 1000 metres, and it is written km. When you read a sentence about a distance, look for the number and the unit. «Light reaches you almost instantly, but sound travels only about 1 kilometre in 3 seconds.» The word kilometre tells you the distance is long, much longer than a metre.
explain: You can picture a kilometre by thinking about walking. It takes about 12 to 15 minutes to walk one kilometre. A school field might be a few hundred metres long, so a kilometre is a lot further. Ask yourself: is this distance short, like metres, or long, like kilometres?
explain: Kilometres are used on road signs, on maps and in speed limits. «Asia is the largest continent, with about 44 million square kilometres.» Here the word is used for area, so you see that kilometres can measure how big a whole piece of land is. Check the word after it to see whether it means distance or square area.
fact: A kilometre is a unit for long distances.
fact: One kilometre is 1000 metres.
fact: Kilometre is written as km.
fact: A kilometre takes about 12 to 15 minutes to walk.
fact: «Kilometres per hour», written km/h, tells you how fast something travels.
exercise: How many metres make one kilometre? | 10 | 100 | 10000 | *1000
exercise: «Light reaches you almost instantly, but sound travels only about 1 kilometre in 3 seconds.» Roughly how long does it take to walk one kilometre? | 1 minute | *12 to 15 minutes | 30 seconds | 2 hours
exercise: Find and copy the short written form of kilometre from this sentence: «Speed signs show 50 km/h in town.» | 50 | signs | town | *km
test: «The deepest fish ever filmed was a snailfish at over eight kilometres.» Is eight kilometres more or less than eight metres? | The same as one metre | Exactly eight metres | Less, under eight metres | *More, over eight thousand metres
test: «A nautical mile is a bit under 2 kilometres.» Is a nautical mile longer or shorter than one kilometre? | The same length | Exactly 10 metres | *Longer, nearly two kilometres | Shorter, under half a kilometre
exam: A speed sign says 60 km/h. What does km/h mean? | Kilograms per hour | Kilometres per minute | Metres per hour | *Kilometres per hour
